echo '<section class="card"><p>The Claims Returned site helps consortium library staff coordinate searches for items patrons report as returned but that are not yet showing as checked in. Staff can look up Alma patron accounts and checked-out items, open and track cases, record search results, and communicate case outcomes.</p><p>Alma remains the source of truth for patron and circulation records. Search notes are saved to the patron record in Alma. When patron email updates are enabled, email is sent when a case opens, closes, or reopens.</p></section>';

echo '<section class="card"><h2>Using the site</h2><ol><li><strong>Sign in</strong> with your consortium staff account.</li><li><strong>Open a case.</strong> Choose New case, enter the patron ID, and look up their account.</li><li><strong>Choose the item.</strong> Select the matching checked-out item from the patron’s loan list. Its details fill the case form.</li><li><strong>Set up the case.</strong> Confirm the patron and item details. Choose the case type, patron email preference, assigned staff member, and any partner library details. Submit the case.</li><li><strong>Complete each search.</strong> On the case page, enter the search result, notes, and due date, then save. Search notes are added to Alma. The patron is not emailed after each search.</li><li><strong>Finish or reopen the case.</strong> Mark the item as found to close the case, or complete the fourth search as not found. If email updates are enabled, the patron receives the final outcome. Reopen a closed case if more searching is needed; the patron is notified when it is reopened.</li><li><strong>Review the queues.</strong> The queue lists active cases. Use Closed cases to view completed cases. Select a case to review its progress, activity, patron account, and contact details.</li></ol></section>';

echo '<section class="card"><h2>User</h2><p>A User can create, view, and update cases for their assigned institution.</p><ol><li>Look up the patron and select the item from their checked-out list.</li><li>Open the case, choose its type, and optionally assign an active staff account.</li><li>Record search outcomes and notes as each search is completed.</li><li>Update assignments, search dates, and patron contact preferences from the case page.</li><li>View the patron’s Alma details and add a custom internal Alma note when needed.</li></ol></section>';

echo '<section class="card"><h2>Super User</h2><p>A Super User can manage cases across institutions. In the queue, use the institution filter to view one institution or all institutions.</p><ol><li>Create and manage cases for any active institution.</li><li>Assign active staff accounts and update case workflow details.</li><li>View open and closed cases across the consortium and reopen cases when necessary.</li><li>Delete individual Alma patron notes when required.</li></ol><p>Super Users do not manage staff accounts.</p></section>';

echo '<section class="card"><h2>Admin</h2><p>An Admin has all Super User case-management access and can also manage user accounts.</p><ol><li>Open Admin from the site navigation.</li><li>Find accounts by name, email, or institution, or look up a staff member by Alma user ID.</li><li>Create accounts, assign an institution and role, edit account details, disable accounts, or set a replacement password.</li><li>Use the case page to delete a case or delete an individual Alma patron note when needed.</li></ol></section>';

